xnu 0390: the root's free space, one line per boot

A full root fails quietly here. `mondrian_root_write` opens the target with
O_TRUNC, the write that follows fails with ENOSPC, and the file stays empty -
while the host counts the datagrams it sent and reports every byte delivered.
Measured twice on 2026-11-20: a dylib injected at exec was 0 bytes on the
phone, dyld had nothing to load, and the process simply ran the old code. The
same volume also refused the launchd table and every log the port wanted to
read back.

So the mount prints what is left: free KiB, total KiB and free inodes, right
after /private/var/vm is confirmed. It is three numbers on a boot that already
prints twenty, and it turns "the write failed and nothing said so" into a
reading.
diff --git a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
index 47c788a..166e7cb 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
@@ -2328,6 +2328,30 @@ mondrian_root_fixups(void)
 		error = mondrian_root_mkdir("/private/var/vm", 0755);
 		printf("MONDRIAN ROOT: mkdir /private/var/vm -> %d\n", error);
 	}
+	/*
+	 * How much room the volume has. A full root does not fail loudly: a
+	 * write is created empty and its data is dropped with ENOSPC, and the
+	 * next boot loads a file that is 0 bytes (measured 2026-11-20, twice,
+	 * while a dylib upload kept reporting every byte delivered). One line
+	 * per boot turns that into a number.
+	 */
+	{
+		struct vfsstatfs *sfs;
+		mount_t rmp = NULL;
+
+		if (vnode_lookup("/", 0, &vp, ctx) == 0) {
+			rmp = vnode_mount(vp);
+			vnode_put(vp);
+		}
+		sfs = rmp != NULL ? vfs_statfs(rmp) : NULL;
+		if (sfs != NULL) {
+			printf("MONDRIAN ROOT: %llu KiB free of %llu KiB, "
+			    "%llu inodes free\n",
+			    (unsigned long long)(sfs->f_bavail * sfs->f_bsize / 1024),
+			    (unsigned long long)(sfs->f_blocks * sfs->f_bsize / 1024),
+			    (unsigned long long)sfs->f_ffree);
+		}
+	}
 #if __has_include("mondrian_glblob.h")
 	{
 		int blob = 0;
